---
description: Python implementation and documentation conventions
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use `from __future__ import annotations` and type annotations for new Python modules and public functions.
- Keep code comments/docstrings in English. User-facing UI text may remain Russian.
- Comments explain non-obvious constraints; do not narrate the next line.
- Preserve module boundaries: core has no network/browser dependency; platform code does not parse legal documents; scenarios do not prompt or print; CLI does not own extraction/business logic.
- Represent extracted values with provenance/confidence/warning fields. Do not silently convert uncertain values to trusted strings.
- Prefer deterministic unit tests, isolated database integration tests and explicit failure injection. Do not make tests contact a live SRO or send personal data externally.
